include LICENSE README.md CHANGELOG.md CONTRIBUTING.md Dockerfile
recursive-include examples *.py *.sh *.xml *.md
# Everything the suite reads, not only the Python: the sdist ships the tests, so
# `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` has to pass from an unpacked one, and
# that is what CI's `distribution` job does with it (#163). A sample or fixture
# whose extension is missing here is a test that cannot run, and the suite used
# to lose 98 of them to the NACHA `.ach` files alone.
recursive-include tests *.py *.xml *.sql *.md *.txt *.ach *.json *.go
# The tests import all five tools and read what they check, and the release
# tools' own tests read the workflow they reason about.
recursive-include tools *.py
recursive-include docs *.md
recursive-include .github/workflows *.yml
